schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: DAO Tooling Landscape
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    Tours the software categories a DAO needs — governance/voting (Snapshot,
    Tally, OpenZeppelin Governor, Aragon), treasury management (Gnosis Safe,
    XDAO), contributor compensation (Coordinape), and DAO-creation platforms
    (Colony, Juicebox, Boardroom, DAOstack) — with recommended starting setups
    and a note that DAOs collectively manage over $30 billion in assets across
    13,000+ organizations.
  audience: DAO-Operator
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      recommended-signer-thresholds (3-of-5 under $10M, 4-of-7 for larger
      treasuries) trade speed of execution against concentration-of-control
      risk.
    - >-
      peer-allocated compensation (Coordinape) vs manager-decided compensation
      — framed as aligned with regenerative, non-hierarchical values.
  related_concepts:
    - multisig-treasury-management
  related_resources:
    - Snapshot
    - Tally
    - Gnosis Safe
    - Coordinape
    - Aragon
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/dao-tooling.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-fda5b8111b9b
  source_lineage: dao-tooling.md
  notes: >
    # assessed-but-excluded

    - XDAO, Juicebox, Colony, Boardroom, DAOstack, OpenZeppelin Governor are
      named with one or two sentences each; not built out as separate resource
      objects (kept the five given the deepest, multi-paragraph treatment —
      Snapshot, Tally, Gnosis Safe, Coordinape, Aragon — as resources instead,
      per "small objects, not mega-objects" but avoiding a 10-way resource
      dump for one-line mentions).
    - No people/community profiles, exact locations, or high-risk triggers
      identified — general tool-literacy content; no public-use-boundary
      object created.
